                                "sense_id": "40ca2ddc-b0b4-3517-bd1e-bf295350bc79",
                                "text": "The empty set is not denumerable because it is finite; the rational numbers are, surprisingly, denumerable because every possible fraction can be assigned a natural number and vice versa."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
